.TH DAYTONA-SHELL 1 "November 2026" "Daytona 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
daytona-shell \- Windows NT 4.0-style desktop shell for labwc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B daytona-shell
[\fB\-\-start\-menu\fR | \fB\-\-lock\fR | \fB\-\-screen\-saver\fR | \fB\-\-system\-properties\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR]
.br
.B daytona-shell
\fB\-\-print\-screen\fR | \fB\-\-print\-window\fR [\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B daytona-shell
draws the Daytona desktop on a Wayland compositor with the layer-shell
protocol (labwc): the taskbar with Start button, Start menu, window buttons,
notification area and clock, the desktop, notification balloons and NT's Run,
Shut Down, Taskbar Properties, Display Properties, Mouse Properties and System
Properties dialogs,
the Control Panel, the screen saver and Lock Workstation. It also serves
\fBorg.freedesktop.ScreenSaver\fR, so programs can keep the screen saver off
while they play video.
It is normally started by labwc's autostart file in a Daytona session
(see \fBdaytona-session\fR(1)). Only one shell runs per session.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-start\-menu
Ask the running shell to open or close its Start menu. labwc runs this for the
Windows keys and Ctrl+Esc.
.TP
.B \-\-lock
Ask the running shell to lock the session (Lock Workstation), and return once
it is locked. The shell runs Daytona's locker, which shows NT's Workstation
Locked dialog; press Ctrl+Alt+Delete and type the password to unlock. labwc runs this for Win+L, and \fBswayidle\fR(1), which the
shell starts, before the computer sleeps and for \fBloginctl lock-session\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-screen\-saver
Ask the running shell to start the screen saver chosen in Display Properties.
\fBswayidle\fR(1) runs this after the screen saver's wait.
.TP
.B \-\-system\-properties
Ask the running shell to open System Properties (the computer's operating
system, processor and memory). labwc runs this for Win+Pause.
.TP
.BR \-\-print\-screen " [\fIFILE\fR]"
Ask the running shell to capture every screen at device resolution, as a PNG
image, and copy it to the clipboard, or save it to \fIFILE\fR. labwc runs this
for Print Screen. It returns once the image is in place, and fails if
\fBgrim\fR(1) or \fBwl-copy\fR(1) is missing or the capture fails.
.TP
.BR \-\-print\-window " [\fIFILE\fR]"
As \fB\-\-print\-screen\fR, but only the screen the active window is on (every
screen when no window is active). labwc runs this for Alt+Print Screen. NT
copied only the active window; labwc gives no way to capture one window.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/daytona/daytona.ini
Taskbar, appearance, screen saver and command settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/daytona/colors.ini
The colour scheme, written by \fBdaytona-themetool\fR(1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR daytona-session (1),
.BR daytona-themetool (1),
.BR grim (1),
.BR labwc (1),
.BR swayidle (1),
.BR wl-copy (1)
